  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The basic sentence: A-B-@-@--",
   "texto": [
    "Almost everything you say at first follows this mold: **A は B です** (A is B).",
    "**は** is the particle that marks **de qué se habla** (the theme). Here you read **wa**.",
    "**です** is «be»: it always goes to the end and **no cambia** with the person. It is pronounced «d», almost without the u.",
    "**わたし は アンナ です** = I'm Anna. Word for word: «I'm Anna.»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Profiles for presentation",
   "texto": [
    "**はじめまして** is said the first time you know someone.",
    "After you have finished introducing yourself: **よろしく おねがいします** (literally «I beg you to treat me well.»). It's essential.",
    "The others are added to **さん** behind the name: **たなか さん** (Mr. or Mrs. Tanaka). **Nunca** put it on yourself.",
    "Para la nacionalidad se añade **じん** al país: スペイン → **スペインじん** (español), にほん → **にほんじん** (japonés)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Where you come from",
   "texto": [
    "**スペイン から きました** = I come from Spain. **から** is the «from,» particle.",
    "To ask the name with education: **おなまえ は？** (your name?)."
   ]
  },
